The pdf.js data files:

While it reads a pdf, pdf.js fetches character maps, fonts for pdfs that do not embed their
own, image decoders and a color profile. They come with pdfjs-dist, are copied to
static/pdfjs on every dev and build run, and are not committed. Each folder keeps the
license files it comes with:

cmaps: Adobe, BSD 3-Clause
iccs: CC0 1.0
wasm: openjpeg BSD 2-Clause, jbig2 BSD 3-Clause (PDFium), qcms MIT, QuickJS MIT, and the
pdf.js wrappers around them Apache-2.0, BSD 2-Clause and MIT
standard_fonts: the Foxit fonts are BSD 3-Clause (PDFium). Liberation Sans is GPL 2 with
Red Hat's font exception, the single thing in here that is not MIT or close to it. pdf.js
only uses it to draw a pdf that names Helvetica or Arial without embedding the font, and
the exception means a page drawn with it is not covered by the GPL. Its license text is in
standard_fonts/LICENSE_LIBERATION next to the font.

Fonts are loaded at runtime from Google Fonts and are not redistributed here:
Instrument Serif, JetBrains Mono and Inter, all under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
